 "gaps": [
  "Several cities (Omaha and Lincoln among them) charge a yearly wheel tax of $10 to $370 set by local ordinance; the DMV does not publish a city table, so it is shown as a range.",
  "The motor vehicle tax and fee are set on the MSRP of the vehicle when new; if you do not type it, the engine uses the price, which understates them for a used car.",
  "The $1 tire fee counts every new tire including the spare, so a new car pays $4 or $5 depending on the spare; it is shown as a range.",
  "Plates cost $4.10 each and a passenger car gets two; nothing is charged when you move plates you already own to the new car.",
  "The motor vehicle tax chart read on the DMV site is marked Rev 2019; the Nebraska Legislature statute site could not be reached to compare it with the current text of section 60-3,185.",
  "No dealer documentation fee cap was read in Nebraska law for this release; Nebraska taxes that fee as part of the sale price."
 ],
