 "defaultCounty": "omaha",
 "singular": [
  "Nebraska's motor vehicle tax is a property tax set by the MSRP: a car that listed at $34,000 to $35,999 starts at a $580 base tax [tax-chart].",
  "The base tax falls with age, to 90% in the second year, 51% in the sixth and 7% in the twelfth and thirteenth years, and nothing is due from the fourteenth year [tax-chart].",
  "A separate motor vehicle fee of $5, $20 or $30 depends on the MSRP band and drops to 70% after five years and 35% after ten, but never reaches zero [tax-chart].",
  "The state sales tax is 5.5% and cities may add up to 2%, with Lincoln at 1.75% and Omaha at 1.5% from July 1, 2026 [local-rates].",
  "The address on the registration decides which local sales tax applies to a car, not the dealer's address [form6].",
  "A dealer's document processing charge is part of the taxable sales price, while the trade-in is deducted [form6].",
  "Every passenger registration costs $15 plus $5.50 of add-ons for emergency medical services, the DMV, recreation roads and the county [dmv-fees].",
  "Electric and hydrogen cars pay a $150 alternative fuel fee at each registration, plug-in hybrids $75 [dmv-fees].",
  "In 2025 Nebraska motorists paid about $45 million of city wheel taxes, which range from $10 to $370 a year [mv-2025].",
  "A Nebraska title costs $10 at the county treasurer, and a car from another state needs a $10 sheriff's inspection first [vin-inspection]."
 ],
 "sources": {
